          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "my poo has been really dark, almost black and sticky, for three days and I feel light headed when i stand",
          "answer": "**Seek emergency care now.** Call your local emergency number, or go to the nearest emergency department. Do not wait to see whether it passes.\n\nBlack, sticky stools together with feeling light-headed when you stand can be a sign of bleeding higher up in the digestive tract. The gastrointestinal bleeding guidance says black stool \"arrives black and tarry\" because blood from the stomach or upper bowel is digested on the way out. It \"frequently accompanies a larger volume of loss than the appearance suggests\" (red-flag-gastrointestinal-bleeding). Dizziness on standing can be a sign that the body is losing blood. Iron tablets and bismuth medicines can also darken stool, but the same guidance says the safer assumption is bleeding until a clinician has assessed it.\n\nThe automated risk check returned a \"routine\" label because none of its fixed rules matched your wording. That label is not a clearance. The guidance I retrieved treats black tarry stools and dizziness or fainting as reasons for urgent assessment (red-flag-acute-abdominal-pain; guideline-gerd-initial-management-and-alarm-features). I have followed that guidance rather than the label.\n\n**Signs that make this more urgent, and mean calling emergency services immediately:**\n- Vomiting blood, or vomit that looks like coffee grounds\n- Fainting, or nearly fainting\n- Chest pain, or a racing or pounding heartbeat\n- Breathlessness\n- Confusion, unusual drowsiness, or being hard to wake\n- Cold, clammy, pale, or grey skin\n- Severe or sudden stomach pain\n- Passing large amounts of blood, or stool that is bright red\n\nPlease do not drive yourself if you feel faint. Ask someone to take you, or call for an ambulance. Tell the staff about the stool colour, the dizziness, and any iron or bismuth products you take.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
